The rewrite closes the two headline wording failures, but several of its new “mechanisms” are still promises without an enforceable design. The most serious issue I’m testing now is whether the central controller, signer, builder, or record service can each defeat the claimed separation—and whether an unreviewed authority description can falsely make a component look safe.
The prior findings and rewritten architecture are now mapped. I am testing whether the stated boundaries survive compromise and cross-component seams.
